# DBT-000 — Debt title

> **Summary:** The defect, measured or named, that the rest of the corpus
> currently assumes is true.
> **Epistemic:** What we lose by not knowing this — the surface a reader
> could misread as complete.
> **Pragmatic:** What closes this entry, and what evidence would prove it.
> **Audience:** Agents

---

## The defect

What is wrong or missing, stated as a fact — not a grievance, not a task. A
debt entry is not a mission; it is the *reason* a mission might exist.

## Evidence

The command, measurement, or citation that proves the defect is real today.
An unverified debt is a rumour with an identifier.

## Closure condition

What must be true for this entry to flip from `active` to `resolved`. Debt
closes, never deletes (ADR-030): the record of what was once wrong is the
point.

